  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.GoogleDrive.Title">Google Drive</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.GoogleDrive.Intro">Connect to Drive files through ADB Player using your own OAuth application.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.GoogleDrive.Step1">1. Create a project in Google Cloud Console and enable the Google Drive API.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.GoogleDrive.Step2">2. Configure the OAuth consent screen, then create an OAuth client of type Desktop application.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.GoogleDrive.Step3">3. Copy the Client ID and Secret into ADB Player's connection dialog or Settings, then sign in with Google.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.GoogleDrive.Note">Google's OAuth testing mode and Drive permissions may have restrictions. Using your own client does not exempt you from Google's policies.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.Dropbox.Title">Dropbox</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.Dropbox.Intro">Your own Dropbox app is recommended; the shared rclone client may face rate limits.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.Dropbox.Step1">1. Create an application in the Dropbox App Console.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.Dropbox.Step2">2. Configure file permissions and the OAuth redirect URL required by the rclone guide.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.Dropbox.Step3">3. Enter the App Key and App Secret in ADB Player, then authorize your account in the browser.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.Dropbox.Note">Personal credentials are recommended. Leaving both fields blank may allow the shared rclone client to connect.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.OneDrive.Title">OneDrive</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.OneDrive.Intro">You can use a personal OAuth application for your Microsoft or work account.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.OneDrive.Step1">1. Register an application in Microsoft Entra admin center.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.OneDrive.Step2">2. Set the redirect URI, account type and permissions according to the rclone guide.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.OneDrive.Step3">3. Enter the client ID and generated client secret in ADB Player, then sign in with Microsoft.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.OneDrive.Note">Work accounts may require admin consent. Personal credentials are recommended; shared rclone defaults may be available.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.PCloud.Title">pCloud</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.PCloud.Intro">Connect a pCloud account in its US or Europe region.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.PCloud.Step1">1. Check whether the official pCloud developer portal offers app creation for your account.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.PCloud.Step2">2. If available, create your application credentials and verify its region and redirect settings.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.PCloud.Step3">3. Enter the app credentials in ADB Player and authorize pCloud in your browser.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="R5165.Guide.PCloud.Note">New pCloud app creation may be unavailable for some accounts. If so, a shared rclone connection may still be possible.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.Title">Cloud &amp; Web Cache</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.Help">Cloud videos are streamed; this section manages temporary rclone disk files only.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.Quota">Cache limit (GB)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.Automatic">Automatically clean old files</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.SafeNote">When over the limit, auto-cleanup removes rclone temp files unused for at least 24 hours. Cleanup never runs during playback.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.Folder">Temporary rclone folder (location)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Settings.CloudCache.ExtraNote">OAuth accounts, rclone/runtime, explicit downloads and attached audio/subtitle files in remote-cache are never deleted. Restart to activate a new cache folder.</sys:String>
